Q: Next.js 14 App Router: useEffect not running on route change when navigating between dynamic segments A: <p>The correct pattern in Next.js 14 is to move data fetching to a <strong>Server Component</strong>. This eliminates the need for useEffect entirely for the initial data load</p>
<pre><code>export default async function ProductPage({ params }: { params: { id: string } }) {
  const { id } = params;

  // Data fetching happens on the server
  const res = await fetch(`https://dummyjson.com/products/${id}`);
  const product = await res.json();

  return (
    &lt;div&gt;
      &lt;h1&gt;{product.title}&lt;/h1&gt;
      &lt;p&gt;{product.description}&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to use Jasmine to test if an instance is created? A: <p>The current answer is outdated <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/33054039/5008962">and this answer here</a> shows the modern, recommend way:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>it(&quot;matches any value&quot;, () =&gt; {
  expect(3).toBeInstanceOf(Number);
});
</code></pre>
